{"type":"text","timestamp":1786327601013,"sessionID":"ses_01694f50effeO7QaUtn9ibxe3F","part":{"id":"prt_fe96c0852001mQ1aMHwZDtwuG9","messageID":"msg_fe96bf69b001Vw5UX1GpjDOI1a","sessionID":"ses_01694f50effeO7QaUtn9ibxe3F","type":"text","text":"Biggest: **SME** (88.02%), Lowest: **LAM** (84.37%).\n\n- SME: consumption 2012 = 869537.52, 2013 = 7258151.96, increase = 6388614.44, % = (6388614.44/7258151.96)*100 = **88.02%**\n- LAM: increase = 3650393.45, % = (3650393.45/4326606.13)*100 = **84.37%**\n- KAM: increase = 3577377.86, % = (3577377.86/4224041.47)*100 = **84.69%**\n\nFinal Answer: SME has the biggest percentage increase (88.02%); LAM has the lowest (84.37%)\nEvidence SQL:\n```sql\nWITH agg AS (SELECT c.Segment AS seg, substr(y.Date,1,4) AS yr, SUM(y.Consumption) AS cons FROM yearmonth y JOIN customers c ON y.CustomerID=c.CustomerID WHERE c.Currency='EUR' GROUP BY c.Segment, substr(y.Date,1,4))\nSELECT a.seg, ROUND((b.cons-a.cons)/b.cons*100.0,2) AS pct FROM agg a JOIN agg b ON a.seg=b.seg AND a.yr='2012' AND b.yr='2013' ORDER BY pct DESC\n```","time":{"start":1786327599186,"end":1786327600997}}}
